course: dictionary
lesson: 12724
title: Drafting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Drafting means writing a first, rough version of something that you will improve later. Writers rarely get it right the first time. «Mia wrote a draft of her story in pencil, then made it better.» A draft is that first try.
explain: Drafting is one stage of the writing process: planning, drafting, editing and publishing. «After planning her story, Sam began drafting it on the back of an old sheet.» In the drafting stage, you get your ideas down, and you do not need to worry about perfect spelling yet.
explain: Drafting can also mean making careful drawings, such as plans for a house or a machine. «The engineer spent all morning drafting plans for the new bridge.» Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Drafting means writing a first, rough version that you will improve later.
fact: Draft can be a noun (a first version) or a verb (to write a first version).
fact: The writing process is planning, drafting, editing and publishing.
fact: In design and technology, drafting means making careful drawings, such as plans.
fact: Drafting can also mean choosing people for a team, or calling people into the army in some countries.
exercise: In English lessons, which stage comes straight after planning? | Reading aloud | Publishing | *Drafting | Printing
exercise: «The engineer spent all morning drafting plans for the new bridge.» What is drafting here? | Writing a shopping list | Swimming across a river | *Making careful technical drawings | Shouting at the workers
exercise: The coach says, «We are drafting in two new players for Saturday.» What does drafting in mean? | Sending players home | Writing a letter to the team | Painting the pitch | *Bringing new people into a team
test: Which is the best meaning of drafting a story? | Buying a new notebook | Reading the story to a friend | *Writing a first, rough version that you will improve later | Counting the words
test: Which phrase means the same as «drafting a letter»? | Tearing up an old letter | Reading a letter aloud | *Writing a rough first version of a letter | Posting a letter to a friend
exam: Lily says, «My draft is messy, but I will fix it in the editing stage.» What is Lily's draft? | A drawing of a house | *A first, rough version of her writing | A list of team members | A finished, printed book
